; Tile bitmaps: 256 tiles of 8 bytes
;
; The 8x8 bitmap of each tile number, 8 bytes top to bottom, tile n at $CF00 + 8 * n. #R$976B copies them into the
; pixel-row pages of the redraw buffer (#R$C500). Tiles $00 and $80 are blank ($80 is the background most rooms are
; filled with), $7B is the heart and $7C the cross of the status bar, $E0-$FF are the pieces of the red pentagram of
; room 24 (a block of 6 by 6 cells in its tile map); the rest are the walls, floors and decorations of the rooms and
; are not described tile by tile here (the attributes in #R$CE00 give their colours: for instance the tiles of rows
; $C0-$DF are blue and $20-$2F cave rock in cyan).
